<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2801" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰχμ-ή</span></b> , ἡ, (
			Aeol.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἴχμα</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			<u>AB</u>
			1095
		</span></i>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>point of a spear</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάροιθε δὲ λάμπετο δουρὸς αἰ. χαλκείη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					6.320
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰ. ἔγχεος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					16.315
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> generally,
				<i>point</i>, of arrows, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοξουλκὸς
			αἰ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				239
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγκίστρου, κεράων</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Opp.
				<u>H.</u>
				1.216
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>C.</u>
				2.451
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>spear</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				12.45
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δαμασίμβροτος αἰ</span>.
				<i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>O.</u>
				9.79
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς τὴν αἰχμὴν
			ἐτράπετο</span> took to his <i>spear</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				3.78
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰχμῇ εἷλε</span>
			<i>with the spear</i>, i.e. in war, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				5.94
			</span></i>; otherwise rare in Prose, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				4.6.4
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b> metaph. of the
			trident of Poseidon, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				925
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>body of spear-bearers</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>O.</u>
				7.19
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Heracl.</u>
				276
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>war, battle</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κακῶς ἡ αἰ.
			ἑστήκεε</span> the <i>war</i> went ill, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				7.152
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρμένοντας αἰχμᾷ</span>
			standing their ground in <i>battle</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				8.40
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θηρῶν</span>
			<i>with</i> wild beasts, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>HF</u>
				158
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b> metaph. of
			plague, <i>sharpness</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βρωτῆρας
			αἰ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Eu.</u>
				803
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>warlike spirit</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰ. νέων θάλλει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Terp.
					6
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θρέψε δ᾽ αἰχμὰν Ἀμφιτρύωνος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>N.</u>
					10.13
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γυναικὸς αἰ</span>. a woman's
				<i>temper</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				483
			</span></i> (lyr.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ch.</u>
				630
			</span></i> (lyr.; but perh. =
			<i>rule</i>, cf.<i><span class="en">
				<u>Pr.</u>
				406
			</span></i>). (Cf. Lith. <i>jiešmas</i> 'spit'.)</div>
